From 15dd5b5982932d6003b437f4bb4a0685826ee83e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jan=20Zo=C5=84?= <jmmzon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:23:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Compositor: keep the boot splash on screen until the greeter
 draws

If Plymouth is still running (deactivated, its last frame scanned out),
copy each output's current framebuffer before the first modeset and draw it
instead of black, keeping it under the scene until the greeter's surface
covers the output (or 15 s pass). NOCTALIA_GREETER_KEEP_SPLASH=0/1 overrides
the /run/plymouth/pid check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
